A</given-names></name><name><surname>Repetto</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title><italic>Trypanosoma cruzi</italic>: H2 complex and genetic background influence on the humoral immune response against epimastigotes.</article-title><source>Int J Parasitol</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>981</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10980286</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005113-VanOvertvelt1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Overtvelt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Andrieu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Verhasselt</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Connan</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Choppin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title><italic>Trypanosoma cruzi</italic> down-regulates lipopolysaccharide-induced MHC class I on human dendritic cells and impairs antigen presentation to specific CD8(&#x0002b;) T lymphocytes.</article-title><source>Int Immunol</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>1135</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12356679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005113-AlbaSoto1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alba Soto</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Mirkin</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Solana</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Gonzalez Cappa</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title><italic>Trypanosoma cruzi</italic> infection modulates in vivo expression of major histocompatibility complex class II molecules on antigen-presenting cells and Tcell stimulatory activity of dendritic cells in a strain-dependent manner.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>71</volume><fpage>1194</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12595432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005113-Fae1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fae</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Drigo</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cunha-Neto</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ianni</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mady</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalil</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>HLA and &#x003b2;-myosin heavy chain do not influence susceptibility to Chagas' disease cardiomyopathy.</article-title><source>Microb Infec</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>745</fpage><lpage>51</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005113-Borrs1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borr&#x000e1;s</surname><given-names>Borr&#x000e1;s Silvia Garc&#x000ed;a</given-names></name><name><surname>Diez</surname><given-names>Cristina</given-names></name><name><surname>Cotorruelo</surname><given-names>Carlos</given-names></name><name><surname>Pellizon</surname><given-names>Oscar</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>HLA class II DRB1 polymorphism in Argentinians undergoing chronic <italic>Trypanosoma cruzi</italic> infection.</article-title><source>Ann Cln Biochem</source><volume>43(3)</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005113-CruzRobles1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cruz-Robles</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Reyes</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Monte&#x000f3;n-Padilla</surname><given-n